## Database Schema

### Model: {{modelName}}

**Location:** `prisma/schema.prisma`

```prisma
model {{modelName}} {
  id          String    @id @default(cuid())
  userId      String
  user        User      @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id])
  responses   Json
  completed   Boolean   @default(false)
  submittedAt DateTime?
  createdAt   DateTime  @default(now())
  updatedAt   DateTime  @updatedAt
{{#if hasUniqueConstraint}}

  @@unique([userId]) // One response per user
{{/if}}
}
```

### Fields

- **id** - Unique identifier (CUID)
- **userId** - Foreign key to User model
- **responses** - JSON object containing all question responses
- **completed** - Boolean flag (false = draft, true = submitted)
- **submittedAt** - Timestamp when form was submitted (null for drafts)
- **createdAt** - Timestamp when record was created
- **updatedAt** - Timestamp of last update (auto-updated)

### Relationships

- **User** - Many-to-one relationship with User model
{{#if hasUniqueConstraint}}
- **Unique Constraint** - Ensures one response per user
{{/if}}

### Migrations

To apply this schema to the database:

```bash
# Generate Prisma client
npx prisma generate

# Create migration
npx prisma migrate dev --name add-{{formSlug}}-form

# Apply migration to production
npx prisma migrate deploy
```

